Z||000010||mope||04-27-2001||06:52 PM||||that smell concept is wierd!<P>pontiacs do all almost smell the same, my 99 grand prix and my sisters 96 grand am seem to smell like rental cars to me. We bought them both new and never use any air freshner either.<P>I dont know what my fiero smells like yet, ive been doing alot of cleaning and painting, its also at the body shop now for paint, so it will take me till bout halfway thru summer to see what it smells like.<P>Hopefully by then it will smell like mr. mikes leather!<P>mope<P>------------------<BR>=======================<P>-= Silver 86 GT, being restored, and following major things to be done: Mr. Mike's Leather, new steering wheel, paint repair, ebrake repair, take apart and clean everything! <A HREF="http://www.mastergraphics.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mastergraphics.cjb.net</A>  <A HREF="http://www.mope.cjb.net" TARGET=_blank>www.mope.cjb.net</A> <p>[This message has been edited by mope (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pontiaddict||04-27-2001||07:29 PM||||Mine smelled kind of dirty, but I cleaned it today and it smells like wax and all of the different air freshner scents combined. (wild flowers smell)<P>As for each manufacturer having it's own smell.. My friend has his cousins Porshe 944 rotting in his yard, I'd steal the seats out of it if I could stand the smell. (yuk) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'd steal some other parts off of it if I could get away with it. (mmmmmmmm, turbo)||||reg||1
