Z||000013||hugh||04-27-2001||08:19 PM||||I don't usually smell anything unless it's really strong,but way back when I was a kid and California wasn't settled yet my father bought a new Buick.It had the same smell as all new cars did at that time.The smell of the chemicals that were used to glue the headliner on and other various and sundry smells.The chemical odors were so strong they would give you a headache if you were in the car too long.It usually took a few weeks for the smell to go away and the headaches to stop.||||reg||1
